==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael archive <path> [options]
       raphael archive --id <id> [options]

Hide an item and everything inside it.

Archive hides items from ordinary lists and search without deleting them. The
slug stays reserved, and favorites and project active state are retained.

Archiving an item already hidden through a parent adds its own archive cause.
Restoring the parent then leaves this item archived. There is no delete command.

Archive causes print one per line, nearest first: directly, or through the
archived container above the item, then who set the cause in parentheses. (user)
is a cause set with archive; restore removes only that cause, and only on the
item itself. JSON carries each cause as origin, owner and reason.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Address by stable id instead of path.
      --revision <n>
          Revision read previously. When omitted, it is read just before
          sending.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael archive /work/raphael
  raphael archive --id 42
  raphael archive --id 42 --revision 8 --json

Prints:
  The item with its path, revision and archive causes; Unchanged when it was
  already archived. JSON carries `node`, `archiveCauses` and `changed`.

Next: raphael restore --id 42

See also: raphael help restore; raphael help revisions
